                        "entry_id": "d085d95e-ea55-339a-b660-e9a9f8edf403",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Able to sire children; sexually mature."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7461e41f-80ac-475d-b6d8-5acab149b216",
                                "sense_id": "d5270394-0e2a-3706-975a-0222728478f0",
                                "text": "He would not suffer his sonne to marrie hir, being not of ripe yeares nor viripotent or mariable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76242ba2-62f3-4745-b0c6-9aadaf537d34",
                                "sense_id": "d5270394-0e2a-3706-975a-0222728478f0",
                                "text": "Mesmer attributed all the phenomena of animal magnetism to the efflux and the influx of a subtle fluid conceived of as specifically localised in the magnet, but radiating also from stars and planets, sun and moon, the earth and the sky, and most effectively of all from the bodies of healthy and viripotent men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e754b7f3-fd8d-47c9-8682-7bcbccae1299",
                                "sense_id": "d5270394-0e2a-3706-975a-0222728478f0",
                                "text": "It has only been done in times past to supply a peculiar class of servants devoted to the care of the women of viripotent men — or, as in the middle ages, to supply alto voices for the religious services in the Roman Church."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fb1ab5f3-f479-308e-99d6-863d66e7520b",
                        "entry_id": "d085d95e-ea55-339a-b660-e9a9f8edf403",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lusty; virile; full of life and sexual energy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4cd10bc1-ba0c-41e2-b237-5663631b1618",
                                "sense_id": "fb1ab5f3-f479-308e-99d6-863d66e7520b",
                                "text": "Of giving potions to make people love or hate as they please, making the strength of youth impotent, and dead bodies viripotent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c00a8165-064a-424f-a0db-94f74c3d0035",
                                "sense_id": "fb1ab5f3-f479-308e-99d6-863d66e7520b",
                                "text": "All now spent which should have seeded viripotent May."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "36c52c87-f821-446d-9de1-e1f8efa77c66",
                                "sense_id": "fb1ab5f3-f479-308e-99d6-863d66e7520b",
                                "text": "Have you, aged, settled into lesser lights, or have you retained all your viripotent powers?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5bf208a-9b94-4ac3-82bb-c93ca2abee26",
                                "sense_id": "fb1ab5f3-f479-308e-99d6-863d66e7520b",
                                "text": "Through their fiction all these writers proclaim the sexual emancipation of women. Their heroines, albeit to a lesser extent than the viripotent Lea of La Bicyclette bleue, experience sexuality as enabling."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7798865b-d899-41c7-a081-ee2d635572df",
                                "sense_id": "fb1ab5f3-f479-308e-99d6-863d66e7520b",
                                "text": "In recent centuries, the austere Jewish sexual code has fallen on hard times in Christendom, because it cuts athwart the passionate desire of the viripotent human male, especially when young but past adolescence,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ebd08c1c-9aaf-4752-a784-6f1937604071",
                                "sense_id": "fb1ab5f3-f479-308e-99d6-863d66e7520b",
                                "text": "\"Seventh Heaven\" Kathmandu Temple Kiff (tm); a viripotent cannabis alternative for blissful regressions of vexatious depressions."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
